<div style="text-align: center">

# <span style="color: #e6a050">Grimoire - Spells and Arrows Slots</span>

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

*<span style="color: #e6a050">Why would you keep a Blizzard in your backpack ?</span>*

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

*The source code for all my Enshrouded mods is available on [GitHub](https://github.com/Fuzen777/Enshrouded-Mods) (MIT)*

</div>

---

Grimoire is a **Kiln** mod that keeps your spells and arrows in a grimoire of their own instead of your backpack. Each kind of spell or arrow gets one slot, the HUD's spell and arrow lists follow the order you set, and picking one in the HUD equips it as usual.

This means you can place spells you use often next to each other or group them thematically, and the order will never move around randomly.

It works with the game's own equipment, not around it, so it doesn't always behave the way you might expect. **Please read the Caveats below before you install it.**

---

## Caveats

### The Equipped One Still Takes a Backpack Slot

- The game only casts a spell (or fires an arrow) from your backpack or hotbar, so **the equipped spell and the equipped arrows each keep one slot there**. Everything else stays in the grimoire. You can put the spell in your hotbar as visual reminder of which arrow/spell you currently have equipped.
- Switching swaps the new pick into that same slot and puts the old one back in the grimoire, so you never need more than that one slot.
- With nothing equipped and a **full backpack**, a spell can't be equipped from the grimoire. Free one slot.
- If the equipped spell sits on your hotbar, it stays there, and the spells you switch to take its place. When switching extremely fast, it can move to another hotbar slot, but it is always just that one spell. This shouldn’t happen anymore.

### Multiplayer and Dedicated Servers

- Grimoire works in **single player**, in **co-op** and on **dedicated servers** (since 1.0.2). In multiplayer, **the server (or the host) needs Grimoire too**, and each player who wants a grimoire installs it as well.
- Each player has their own grimoire, order and settings. Players without Grimoire on their game are left alone.
- **Dedicated servers haven't been tested in game yet.** Grimoire is built for them, but if something doesn't work on yours, please report it with your kiln.log from the server and from your game.

### What Joins the Grimoire by Itself

- Any spell or arrow **already in your grimoire** that shows up in your backpack (looted, crafted, picked up, or the one you just switched away from) is filed into the grimoire within about a second, unless it is the equipped one.
- Spells and arrows you never added stay in your backpack. By default they are **hidden from the HUD** (see **Hide Other Spells And Arrows** below): turn that off to pick them from the HUD again. Picking one puts the grimoire's equipped one back in the grimoire.
- **Take Out** (RMB in the grimoire window) removes a spell from the grimoire for good, so it stops being filed in again.

### Removing the Mod

- Kiln keeps the grimoire's contents with your character, **outside the backpack**. Without Grimoire installed, they stay stored but out of reach until you install it again.
- **Before you uninstall**, open the grimoire (F3) and press **Take All Out** on both the Spells and the Arrows tab, with enough free backpack slots. Then save.
- Turning **Mod Enabled** off brings back the game's own lists, but the grimoire keeps what it holds. Take everything out first if you want it back in your backpack.

### HUD Lists

- The HUD shows only the grimoire's spells, in your order, plus the one you have equipped if it isn't in the grimoire. With **Hide Other Spells And Arrows** off, the other spells in your backpack follow them.
- When the list has hidden itself, moving to one of the grimoire's spells doesn't bring it back the way moving to a backpack spell does. The pick still works. That's a Kiln limit (reported).
- While you switch spells very quickly, the game sometimes empties the spell slot for a moment. Grimoire puts the spell back, so you may see the HUD flash no spell for a split second.

### Death

- The grimoire is kept on death. The equipped spell and arrows are in your backpack, so the game's own rules apply to them.

### Other Mods

- Don't use it together with another mod that changes the HUD's spell or arrow list, like **Quiver &amp; Spellbook**. If you're replacing Quiver &amp; Spellbook, move its hidden spells and arrows back into your backpack and save **before** you remove it, or they will be lost.

---

## Features

### Grimoire Window

- Opens with **F3** (or the **Open Grimoire** button on the mod's page in Kiln's menu), with a **Spells** tab and an **Arrows** tab. It opens on Spells, unless you only have arrows to sort.
- Move it and resize it as you like: it opens where you left it, at the same size, even after a restart. **Esc** or **F3** closes it.
- With **Better Spells** (1.3.0 or newer) installed, the grimoire and Better Spells' settings window open side by side, even on the same key, and move together (Kiln **0.2.0-dev.31.16 or newer**). Hold **Shift** while dragging to move one alone, and drop it back beside the other to join them again.
- Click an entry to equip it, drag to reorder, RMB (or drag it onto the backpack list) to take it out.
- The spells or arrows in your backpack are listed below: click one or drag it in to add it. **Ctrl + LMB** a spell or arrow in the game's inventory adds it too. **Add All** and **Take All Out** move everything at once.

### Settings

- **Mod Enabled**: off gives you the game's own lists back. The grimoire keeps what it holds.
- **Hide Other Spells And Arrows** (on by default, below the backpack list of each tab): the HUD lists show only what is in the grimoire, and the one you have equipped. Off: the other spells and arrows in your backpack come after the grimoire's.
- **Spell Slots** and **Arrow Slots** (1 to 32, default 12): how many kinds the grimoire holds, one slot each. More of a kind already in it tops up its slot. Lowering it keeps what is already in it.

### Running Out

- When a charged spell or a stack of arrows runs out, more of the same is equipped from the grimoire, otherwise the next one in your order.

---

## Requirements

- [Kiln](https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln) mod loader, **0.2.0-dev.31 or newer** (Kiln's player storage).
- In multiplayer: Kiln and Grimoire on the server (or the host) and on each player's game that wants a grimoire.
- Opening side by side with Better Spells: Kiln **0.2.0-dev.31.16 or newer**. With an older Kiln, each window opens where you left it.

## Installation

1. Close the game.
2. Drop the archive on Kiln.
3. Start the game and load your world, or join a server that runs Grimoire.
4. Press F3, then add your spells and arrows.

**Changing the key**: it is **Open Grimoire** in the Keys tab of Kiln's menu. The settings are kept in Kiln's profile, so updating the mod never resets them.

---

